* VALID_OS_PATH(path)
* Return @true if path is safe to embed in OS.EXECUTE chmod-style commands.
* Copyright (c) String Database
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 14 Aug 26 Windows port - accept backslashes and spaces, so that native
*                      Windows paths pass.  The caller quotes.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    x = !valid_os_path(path)
*
*    Rejects empty paths, excessive length, and shell metacharacters while
*    allowing directory separators - both of them - and spaces.
*
*    THE CALLER MUST SINGLE QUOTE THE PATH.  OS.EXECUTE runs the command
*    through "/bin/bash -c" (op_sh.c), so a path containing a space is two
*    words unless it is quoted.  Single quotes, not double: inside double
*    quotes bash still treats a backslash as an escape, so a path ending in a
*    separator would escape the closing quote.  Inside single quotes nothing
*    is special, and the apostrophe that would end the quoting is not in the
*    permitted set, so it cannot be reached.
*
*    That is the whole reason spaces are now allowed.  The rejection was
*    deliberate - unquoted, a space is a shell metacharacter - but it also
*    rejected every path under C:\Program Files, which is where SD's binaries
*    go (PROJECT_STATUS.md section 5.8).  Quoting at the call site is the
*    protection; the character set is what is left over.
*
*    Still rejected, and these are the ones doing the work: ; & | < > $ `
*    quotes of either kind, brackets and braces, * ? ~ ! # and whitespace
*    other than a plain space.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function valid_os_path(path)
$catalog !valid_os_path

   * Modified by Composer AI - 2026/06/10.
   * Shared pathname validation for OS.EXECUTE (phase 2).
* 14 Aug 26 Windows port - backslash and space added.  See the description.
   path.chars = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789._-/:\ '
   if path = '' then return @false
   if len(path) > 255 then return @false
   if convert(path.chars, '', path) # '' then return @false
   * --------------------
   return @true

end

* END-CODE
